Z||000000||ragilmore||09-10-2001||11:44 AM||||My 88 formula's oil guage peg's when I turn on the key Have checked sending unit it's ok any help? Thank's Richard  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-10-2001||02:02 PM||||If the gage pegs and <B>stays</B> pegged when you switch the ignition on, that tends to say that there's a break (an "open") somewhere in the circuit from the gage to the sender.  First place to look is the easiest - at the connector that plugs into the sending unit.  Try momentarily grounding the <B>center</B> terminal with a <B>fused</B> jumper.  The oil pressure gage should respond.<P>Be careful! - One of the 3 terminals in the oil pressure sender's connector is <B>always</B> hot - whether or not ignition is switched on.  ||||reg||4
